            <div xml:id="d343">

                <pb facs="0358" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg349"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.5151/1113: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-03T14:00:00-03:00">June 3, 1938—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 3—2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>135. My 116, May 19, 7 p.m.<anchor n="26" xml:id="d343-f1"/> I have been informed
                    confidentially by the Foreign Office today that several European nations are
                    bringing pressure to bear in order to receive treatment similar to that accorded
                    to drafts covering merchandise of United States origin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
